    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0543" n="463" xml:id="pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5532/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-05T15:00:00-03:00">December 5, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 5—2:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>162. Department’s 94, December 3, 6 p.m. Since my telegram No. 161, December 5, 2
                        p.m.,<anchor n="26" xml:id="d497-f1"/> transmits formal notice that the
                    services of the Naval Mission will terminate on January 31st next, I shall be
                    gratified if Lieutenant Commander Blandy’s appointment can be announced. The
                    effect here will be beneficial.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d497-f1" n="26" xml:id="d497-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see despatch No. 3475, December 5, from the Ambassador in Brazil,
